## Verification

{{VERIFICATION_SECTION}}

Follow the established verification contract for the affected area, including required full gates. Inspect script dependencies and lifecycle hooks before composing checks; avoid separate builds, tests, or typechecks already covered. Report automated results, manual review, and actual harness instruction-loading confirmation separately. Passing checks provide evidence; also assess the requested behavior and acceptance criteria.

## Boundaries

- Stay in task scope; no drive-by refactors or unrelated "cleanups".
- No new dependencies without justification and approval.
- Check the branch, commit, and working tree before editing; preserve unrelated changes and follow repository conventions.
- Ask only for essential missing information or material decisions outside the authorized scope; carry existing approvals forward.
- Stage, commit, push, merge, publish, or deploy only when explicitly authorized. Implementation completion does not require Git actions.
- Never modify CI, deployment config, secrets, or environment files without explicit approval.
- Match the style of the file being edited; preserve working behavior.
